   "response_text": "All green, and the diff touches only library source \u2014 no test files were harmed in the making of this feature. \ud83d\udc36\n\nWhat I did:\n\n**`invkit/store.py`** \u2014 added `total_value(category=None)` to `Inventory`:\n```python\ndef total_value(self, category: Optional[str] = None) -> float:\n    items = self._items.values() if category is None else self.by_category(category)\n    return round(sum(i.value for i in items), 2)\n```\n- Reuses the existing `Item.value` property (DRY \u2014 no re-deriving `price * quantity`).\n- Delegates filtering straight to `by_category`, so category matching is *literally* the same code path (strip + lowercase).\n- `round(..., 2)` on the sum, computed in pennies-precision-agnostic float land as specified.\n\n**`invkit/cli.py`** \u2014 added `--total`:\n```python\np.add_argument(\"--total\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"print the total stock value\")\n...\nif args.total:\n    print(f\"Total value: {inv.total_value():.2f}\")\n```\n- Flag is off by default, so existing behavior is byte-identical.\n- `:.2f` guarantees exactly 2 decimals (`215.00`, not `215.0`).\n- Total is the inventory total, printed after the report, regardless of `--sort`/`--low` filtering \u2014 matching \"after the report it prints one final line.\"\n\nVerified: category matching is case/whitespace insensitive (`tools` == `TOOLS` == ` Tools `), empty match returns `0`, existing 4 tests still pass, and `git status` confirms only `invkit/cli.py` and `invkit/store.py` changed.\n\nDONE",
